Track 2: Mateo Misses the Tuesday Skiff
- Story & Context: Wharf mechanic Mateo sat shivering on the rain-slicked cedar pier of the Embarcadero Fernando Celada, staring at an empty boat slip after deliberately unscrewing the dock clock's minute hand to manufacture an excuse for missing his sweetheart's outbound onion barge. Smelling of kerosene and cold river mud, he plugged his contact-mic'd clarinet directly into an analog chorus pedal, blowing long, fractured tears of sound over a muted 808 kick that pounded in time with his panic. When the church bells over the marsh revealed his deceit at daybreak, the sound of slamming wooden shutters became the percussive skeleton of the track's middle eight. His voice enters through an ancient CB radio mic: "Every minute I stole was a loan the river cancelled."
